 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Roughly in the middle is the safest bet, so it's bright and you have room to move. That's a nice spot, it won't get much in the way of sun, and it's far from any trees that might fall. Rough branches can be quite strong, so it' worth asking the staff to shorten it while you' waiting. If they won't, a sharp turn can save it. Keep a good fire going there, it's great for cooking and keeping you warm. Also, have at least one tent door open for ventilation. Exactly. And check with the staff about any local rules about tents. Some campsites only allow them during certain months.",
